  </worksheets>
  <dashboards>
    <dashboard _.fcp.AccessibleZoneTabOrder.true...enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Definitions'>
      <repository-location derived-from='https://tableau.deliveryhero.net/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/VendorMarkupBehavior/Definitions?rev=' id='Definitions' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/VendorMarkupBehavior' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style />
      <size maxheight='1000' maxwidth='1200' minheight='1000' minwidth='1200' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='98400' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98666' x='667' y='800'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='18'>Vendor Markup Behavior Dashboard </run>
              <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='18'>Methodology and KPIs</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>This dashboard focuses on the price change behavior of vendors before, during and after campaigns. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Scope of Data:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Only </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>vendors</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> with shoptype &quot;food&quot; which had at least 150 orders monthly during the last 6 months period.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Campaigns</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> created/expired in the last 12 Months</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='15' underline='true'>Methodology</run>
              <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>In order to understand the behavior of increase/decreasing prices relative to campaign timeframe, analysis was conducted by matching product price timeframes with campaign timeframes:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Pre campaign </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>           = Last 7 days before the campaign</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Campaign window </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> = During the campaign</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Post campaign</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>           = Preceding 7 days after the campaign</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Hourly average product prices</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> during these 3 time-frames per </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>campaign</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> were compared, in order to decide for Markup Behavior. Also for </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Order</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> and </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>GMV incr</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>, </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>daily averages</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> of these KPIs per vendor was compared in order to understand the additional effect of the campaigns.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>To keep in mind: One vendor can have multiple campaigns and even one campaign can have multiple product prices. This in turn gives the following KPIs: </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>number of vendors</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>, </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>number of campaigns</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> and </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>number of campaign-product pairs</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='15' underline='true'>Measures/KPIs and Definitions:</run>
              <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Number of vendors: </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>This KPI shows the number of vendors which had at least one behavior type  </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>campaign-product</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>. Meaning the number of times/</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>campaigns/products</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> this behavior occured is not taken in to account in this KPI.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Number of campaigns: </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>This KPI shows the number of campaigns which had at least one behavior type  </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>campaign-product</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>. Meaning the number of times/products this behavior occured is not taken in to account in this KPI.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Number of campaign-products: </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>This KPI shows the number of campaign-product pairs which had the behavior type  </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>campaign-product</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>. Meaning that product numbers can be </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>duplicated</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> if they had the </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>same treatment in different campaigns</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Thereso, when in to dashboard, checking the specific behavior on different levels, the analyzing team decided to look for </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>number of vendors</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'> for </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>entity level</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>, and number of </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>campaigns/campaign-products </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>when diving in to </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>more granular vendor level</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>% KPIs focus on the % share of specific behavior regarding that KPI level (vendor/campaign/campaign-products). For instance:  </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11' italic='true'>% Campaign Products Camp Window Increase </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>means: </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>[ the number of campaign-product pairs with Behavior 2]   /    [total number of campaign-product pairs]</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
